01 NCAC 01B .0601  SUBJECTS OF DECLARATORY RULINGS  
(a) Any person substantially affected by a statute or rule administered by the Department of Administration may request a declaratory ruling as to the validity of an agency rule or as to either the manner in which a statute or rule applies to a given factual situation.  
(b) A declaratory ruling issued by the agency:  
 (1) is binding upon the agency and upon the person requesting it;  
 (2) may be reviewed by the courts in the same manner as the final agency action in a contested case; and  
 (3) may be altered by a subsequent declaratory ruling of the agency, but may not be altered retroactively.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
